hint  `enth params <kind>` lists a kind's parameters with units and ranges

builtins:
  key     params  summary
  voice   5       The voice manager and amp stage: mode (poly, mono, legato), polyphony, glide, pan; voice.amp_env names the amplitude envelope.
  master  1       The output stage after the effects: level in dB.

modules:
  kind    section     id_prefix  params  summary                                                                                                         name        tier
  osc     generators  osc        11      A pitched tone: sine, triangle, saw, pulse with width, or a wavetable, with hard sync to the first oscillator.  Oscillator  basic
  noise   generators  noise      2       Unpitched hiss, white or pink, for breath, attack transients and texture.                                       Noise       intermediate
  svf     voice_fx    filter     5       A resonant multimode filter per voice: shapes brightness, usually swept by an envelope.                         Filter      basic
  adsr    modulators  env        5       An attack-decay-sustain-release envelope per note, 0 to 1; one of them is the voice's amplitude envelope.       Envelope    basic
  lfo     modulators  lfo        7       A slow repeating modulator for vibrato, tremolo and sweeps, per voice or shared by all voices.                  LFO         intermediate
  reverb  fx          reverb     10      A stereo room or hall after the voices: adds space, width and a tail.                                           Reverb      intermediate
  comp    fx          comp       7       Evens out loudness after the voices: turns loud parts down above a threshold, then makes up the gain.           Compressor  advanced

